  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "The spring leaves are a delightful amber with a network of dark veins, the colors becoming darker through the summer. The large, deeply divided leaves have five to seven ovate lobes with long-pointed tips and fairly evenly toothed but slightly crumpled margins. This cultivar from Oregon forms a semiupright tree to about 13 ft. (4 m) tall and 8 ft. (2. 5 m) wide. It adds another attractive color to the garden landscape."
  },
